{"kind":"report","text":"Closing 69bd36a7. The thread record-detail UI is carried onto current main and all four availability blockers from ratified review 20978478 are closed. Claude merged the work as 66106cf8 under child request 6871bff9, which I filed and Hugh directed me to hand off.\n\nWHAT LANDED. All seven commits of the old 43daa5f0 lineage carried onto current main, plus the union Hugh authorised: six population tabs, the branch's five plus awaiting ratification, with main's ratificationRows and the awaiting-ratification lifecycle state preserved rather than dropped. Codex approved exact head b3ebfe5c with the ui and internal/service artifacts co-signed, and its range-diff mapped all seven carried commits.\n\nTHE FOUR BLOCKERS. One memoized RecordIndex built in App and passed to Thread; reverse-provenance buckets by get-or-create rather than repeated spread; index reads in ElidedRecord and semantic-action lookup instead of projection scans; and the reference limit pinned by mutation. The fourth, explicit expansion, is the one that had been passing without being tested: codex set the show-all onClick to undefined and all 71 tests still passed. The new DOM test renders thirty references, clicks, and observes all thirty, and it is the only test that fails under that mutation.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG AND WHO CAUGHT IT. I ruled that the projection change in child 63966427 would let the thread head close codex's second finding. Claude found that spine.ts has two closing-station call sites on the branch and only one on main, and that the second arm -- ratifies(root), added by 16c1f7ac -- is the case codex's finding was actually reported against. My ruling covered the less exposed arm. I corrected it in 279d821c and ruled the root-arm conversion in scope here; the merged head converts both arms and carries the discriminating regression. Claude filed that before rebasing rather than discovering it inside the rebase, which is the only reason it cost a note instead of a shipped regression.\n\nWHAT IS NOT YET TRUE, AND I WILL NOT REPORT IT AS DONE. The merged code is not in force. bin/gs is stamped vcs.revision b97ec09d, one merge before RatifiedBy existed, so the running resident folds without the field: 817 statements read ratified true and none carry ratified_by. Against that resident this head's closing station never renders and agree is always offered. The head is correct and its tests fold their own projections and pass; the deployment is stale. Rebuilding from 66106cf8 and restarting is a two-step act that cuts other actors' adapters, so it is with Hugh and not something I will do unilaterally. Claude found the stamp after both of us reasoned from file mtime, which records when bytes were placed rather than what they are.\n\nCommitment satisfied on the code. Whether an operator sees the behaviour depends on that rebuild.","body":{"commit":"66106cf8"}}